  "verbalization": "Pilosanol N is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular interactions involving Prelamin-A/C. The evidence suggests that Pilosanol N directly targets Prelamin-A/C, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Zeaxanthin dipalmitate and Pseurata C. These intermediates ultimately lead to the activation of Phosphodiesterase 6C. The shared pathway from Pilosanol N to Phosphodiesterase 6C is supported by the high confidence scores in the three distinct paths, indicating a consistent mechanism across different molecular entities. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Prelamin-A/C as a bridge between Pilosanol N and Phosphodiesterase 6C, suggesting that the drug may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate enzyme activity. The evidence underscores the importance of Prelamin-A/C in mediating the interaction between Pilosanol N and Phosphodiesterase 6C, reinforcing the hypothesis that this relationship is driven by a shared biological function.",
